--- surface notes (parity with the web source) ---
- Architecture mirrors the shipped sibling VehicleHero (web VehicleGauges is a presentational child of the
  vehicles page; the native surface binds the same data — GET /vehicles -> resolve primary/explicit vehicle,
  GET /vehicles/{id}/state — through the shared cache-then-network state holder, so EVERY state renders).
- Component mapping (web -> native counterpart; atomic components are out of scope per the prompt):
  GlassPanel->TsGlassPanel; FadeIn->TsFadeIn; MetricBar->TsMetricBar; TeslaCarViz->TsVehicleTwin
  (VehicleTwinModel: Locked/SentryMode/IsCharging/IsDriving(speed>0)/ExteriorColor; parseModelKey surfaced in
  the twin's Narrator name). RadialGauge: drawn from the shared ChartGeometry/ChartShapes primitives (the same
  ones TsRadialGauge uses) — the HealthGaugeGrid precedent — because the web colours each gauge by a SEMANTIC
  value (batteryColor / boolColorMuted), not purely a brand-palette role, and TsRadialGauge.Role has no danger
  hue for the low-SoC red tier.
- Colour fidelity (web hex -> exact design-token brush key): CYAN #00f0ff->TsChartSpeedBrush,
  PURPLE #a855f7->TsChartPowerBrush (exact), GOOD #10b981->TsColorSuccessBrush, WARN #f59e0b->TsColorWarningBrush
  (=TsChartEnergyBrush hue), BAD #ef4444->TsColorDangerBrush, MUTED/DARK->TsColorTextMutedBrush.
- States (all render, never a blank panel): loading (skeleton gauges), loaded (car + 4 gauges + metric bars +
  chips), empty (no vehicle OR no live state -> friendly EmptyState), error (TsQueryError + retry), stale
  (content + stale chip), offline (content + offline chip).
- i18n (every web string keyed through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade; all 13 already in Strings/en/Resources.resw):
  common.battery, common.range, common.speed, common.power, common.batteryLevel, common.estimatedRange,
  common.chargeRate, common.locked, common.unlocked, common.sentryOn, common.sentryOff, common.climateOn,
  common.climateOff (+ native chrome: common.loading/offline/stale/refresh; native-only surfaceName/empty/error
  resolve via the facade's English fallback).
- Accessibility: surface AutomationPeer is a Group named by the composed surface name; each gauge/metric/chip
  carries a Narrator name; decorative glyphs + the gauge canvas are AccessibilityView.Raw; entrances fade via
  TsFadeIn which honours reduce-motion.
- Telemetry: view.opened slug=VehicleGauges on first load, per the P1/S11 diagnostics contract (PII-safe — never
  a VIN, name, location or telemetry value).

